-- ERROR ---------------- errors/duplicate_binder_6.march

`b` is bound twice in the same parameter list or pattern. [duplicate_binder]

5 |     let (b, b) = (3, 4)
                ^

    A parameter list or a pattern binds each name once, so there is no single value this name could refer to.
    Rename one of them, or write `_` for an argument you don't use. To require two values to be equal, bind two names and compare them in a `when` guard: `(b, b2) when b == b2 -> …`.

    first bound here:

5 |     let (b, b) = (3, 4)
             ^
    run `march --explain duplicate_binder`


